  "sections": [
   {
    "heading": "Syncopation",
    "paragraphs": [
     "A syncopation is a note that is placed on the weak beat instead of the strong one. It must be held for its whole value, making its starting point well felt; but in no case must the second part of its value be heard as a jolt.",
     "Play it with one attack for each note, tu tu tu tu tu tu, and not ta, ta-a, ta-a, ta-a, ta, ta."
    ]
   }
  ],
